{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the repaired room proof reuse at head ef19d1ffb95e16b5973426d66473d2cc64bb1d41, tree b12bc550, for request 7c0e8181 and review request 9214f19a. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nThe head adds two commits to the reviewed head 57fb1988. I read the rewritten implementation note first, then the diff from 57fb1988, against items 1 and 2 of review 06820307. The production change is in `packages/replay/src/verify.ts`, and the only test change appends two cases to `packages/replay/test/room-recovery.test.ts`. The rest of the head is unchanged, and the findings of 06820307 on reuse, accounting, the witness and the contract text stand.\n\n## Items of 06820307\n\n1. A later blocked position hid an earlier problem. Resolved.\n   - The new `#recordProblem` (`verify.ts:672-677`) replaces a scope's problem only with one that starts earlier. Every write to `#blocked` and to the final problem map now goes through it: the refresh conflict, the floor mismatch, a failed step, the owed debts, the historical-byte retractions, unwalked records and incomplete byte spans.\n   - The spread (`verify.ts:747-748`) queues a dependent only when its problem moves earlier, which keeps the old stop rule.\n   - A debt keeps the settlement's finding as its stop. In the new case, the room therefore reports the mismatch at entry 3 for a use at entry 2, as a standalone `verify` does.\n   - The case \"an earlier missing text remains a problem below a later blocked entry\" checks the standalone and the room results side by side. Its control restores the first-written rule, and the room then answers `consistent` where `mismatch` is required, an ordinary AssertionError.\n2. The room settlement recovered missing texts for definitions without capacity. Resolved.\n   - The new `#canRecoverDebt` (`verify.ts:656-658`) puts the capacity check, `#recoverableText` and the numeric size into one predicate. Both `#recoverRoomDebts` and the standalone `#settle` use it.\n   - The standalone result is unchanged: `#settle` returned early without capacity before, and the shared predicate now refuses each digest instead.\n   - The other callers of `#recoverableText` are the same as at 5c6ea9bb. The room-only re-judgment at `verify.ts:2342` reads only text sizes, and it cannot clear a debt.\n   - The case \"a source without capacity still owes its missing text when another root holds the body\" reads the body from a second root. The room reports `incomplete` at the same fact as a standalone `verify`. Its control removes the capacity term, and the room then answers `consistent`, an ordinary AssertionError.\n   - Both controls restore the source.\n\n## The gates\n\n- Gates 1 and 2 stay failed, and gate 3 at G stays a pass for that source.\n- The repair changed production source, so ruling 31962e1f needed one further full gate. Gate 4 at I, 01361742 with tree b5088359, passes all five stages. Its receipt has SHA-256 fc1141fd, exit 0, and the same head and tree before and after.\n- Gate 4 runs the 2,000-member room case again at I, and it passes in 155 seconds.\n- I to the head changes only the note and the manifest, which the documents-only rule in `docs/testing.md` covers.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree is clean. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 5c6ea9bb gives the head tree b12bc550.\n- I reran `room-recovery.test.ts` and `room-verification.test.ts` once each, with no whole suite: 15 of 15. The builder worktree stayed clean after the run.\n- The original three recovery cases and every replay test file on main are unchanged.\n- The manifest has SHA-256 83859bb0 and 31,650 bytes. It follows ruling 4e199bd8 for both roots:\n  - repair root: all 32 listed files match by size and SHA-256; `finalization` and `operator-inputs` match their digests, with no unlisted file; the root SHA256SUMS, digest 1ef4a647, covers all 1,002 other files, with none unlisted and none writable;\n  - the original root, under `priorEvidence`: the manifest digest is still 9c5056e4, all 168 listed files match, and its root SHA256SUMS still has digest d2caa18f.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 760 links, 0 broken.\n- check-notes from 5c6ea9bb: 0 warnings.\n- check-commit-messages from 5c6ea9bb: 10 checked, 0 flagged.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n- All 17 artifacts at the head are current, and none is stale.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. Each scope keeps one problem, which is the earliest. If an unwalked record or a missing text comes before a mismatch in the same scope, the room reports `incomplete` where a standalone `verify` reports the mismatch first. Neither answer is `consistent`, so the result stays sound.\n2. The two points of 06820307 remain: the union can drop the origin of a shared text, and a rebuild re-checks a sealed prefix without charging entries.\n3. The note is now hard to read in another way. Many sentences are fragments without their subject (\"Receipts retain A.\"). The note also uses \"H\" for two things: the control's source 80749894 and the reviewed head 57fb1988.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe repair stays inside the room settlement. One rule now decides recovery for both proofs, and one rule decides which problem a scope keeps. The repair removes the repetition that review 06820307 named. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\n`dap verify --all` no longer reports a scope consistent when a later block hides an earlier problem, or when another root holds a text that a definition without capacity owes. Each fix has a case that compares the room with a standalone `verify`, and a control. Approved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe repair adds 32 lines and removes 16 in `verify.ts`. It replaces four ad hoc merge rules with one helper, and two recovery conditions with one predicate. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: items 1 and 2 of 06820307 hold in the source, the two new cases, their controls and gate 4. Reuse, the unchanged defaults, unique-entry accounting, the default room witness, the accepted prior-head control and the unchanged replay tests hold as in 06820307. The evidence verifies under ruling 4e199bd8 in both roots. Gates 1 and 2 stay failed.\n\nThe landing check will follow the landing. The head regenerates `apps/room/page/assets.ts`, which a Worker imports, so the planner decides on a deploy after the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:140c114251c2f086e6b837afe9741d8e9ec8d18b","binding":"assigned","head":"ef19d1ffb95e16b5973426d66473d2cc64bb1d41","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:84c10f533831bd5ba5a92d86cb648997b923f8a9\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:310185bf8291b7c7d4a373d845a449b6bc374e9a\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:84c10f533831bd5ba5a92d86cb648997b923f8a9","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}